positive_text:
How many functions $f: \mathbb{Z} ightarrow \mathbb{R}$ satisfy the following three properties?
(i) $f(1) = 1$;
(ii) For all $x, y \in \mathbb{Z}$, $f(x)^2 - f(y)^2 = f(x+y) f(x-y)$;
(iii) For all $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, $f(k) = f(k+2013)$.

negatives.text:
