(a) the center of $C_2$ lies on the circle $C_1$;
(b) the four points $M, N, P, Q$ in appropriate order form a square if and only if twice the radius of $C_1$ is three times the radius of $C_2$.

Let triangle $ABC$ have an incircle $C_1$ that touches $AB$ at $D$ and $AC$ at $E$. The incircle $C_2$ of triangle $ADE$ touches $AB$ and $AC$ at $P$ and $Q$, and intersects $C_1$ at points $M$ and $N$. Prove that
